  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strategy Planning Processes 2006/7</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. To enable participatory and consultative processes to be set up and implemented to allow a wide range of partners, other stakeholders, and relevant CAFOD departments and sections to contribute towards the process of developing country strategies and the regional humanitarian strategy.

2. To develop strategies for CAFOD&apos;s Southern Africa regional programme that are in line with CAFOD&apos;s 2010 Building Communities for Change and which take into account country contexts, the present programme and possible direction, the strengths and weaknesses of partner organisations including Church structures and capacities.

3. To document the assessment and analysis and make recommendations in consultation with identified reference groups and stakeholders and in doing so strategise the way forwards including likely resource-needs and associated funding strategies where applicable.</narrative>
  </description>
